Generalization Principle

Instead of optimizing for

\max \text{Knowledge}

optimize for

\max \text{Operator Quality}

because

\text{Knowledge}
=
\sum_i
\Delta_i

while

\text{Operator Quality}
\propto
\frac{d(\text{Knowledge})}{dt}

A better operator doesn’t just produce one better answer—it improves the trajectory of future answers. That’s why abstractions that capture reusable transformations can have disproportionate leverage across domains: they become generators for many future solutions rather than isolated facts.